om2
note intake.om: the Open Humanity intake, its own seeded Omega program. It runs outside the forged
note sandbox, because bringing a project means asking the Radicle node to seed and fetch it, and
note forged has no network and cannot run rad.
note   open-intake <open dir/> <state file> <work dir/> <radicle storage dir/> <home dir> [once]
note open dir: <data>open/ (queue written by forged; list.tsv published here, whole or not at all)
note state:    one decimal number, the queue offset already handled
note work dir: private, outside the folder forged can write: the list this program acts on
note           (list.tsv; the copy in the open dir is only what forged shows, never read back),
note           the allow file and command output
note Queue lines (from a less trusted process, so every field is checked again):
note   B <tab> rid <tab> did <tab> note     bring the project
note   W <tab> rid <tab> did               withdraw it (only the key that brought it)
note A queue read to its end past 262,144 bytes is renamed to queue.old, finished and removed, so
note forged's 1 MiB cap on the queue is never permanent.
note Bring: refused when the key is not in <work dir>allow, when the project is already on the
note shelf, when its storage folder already exists on this node or the node already has a seeding
note policy for it (a repository this node holds or seeds for another reason is never touched),
note when the key has 8 open projects or the shelf has 200. A folder left by this program's own
note failed fetch of the same project is removed first. While the row says that fetch failed, a
note refusal that is not about a fetch (key not invited, quota, node not answering) leaves the row
note as it is, so it cannot turn that leftover into a refusal for good. Then rad seed --scope all --fetch (90 s);
note not found is refused and unseeded; over 51,200 KiB is refused, unseeded and removed. The
note project's name and description come from its Radicle identity document.
note Held: a public project this node already holds (rad inspect --visibility says public) is not
note fetched, seeded or changed; it gets a row in state "held", so the owner of the node and the
note keys it invited can put the node's own unfinished projects on the shelf. Withdrawing a held
note row only marks it; the repository and its seeding policy stay as they were.
note Withdraw: rad unseed, remove the storage folder, mark the row withdrawn. Only a row that is
note "open" in the private list, brought by the same key, can be withdrawn, so this program never
note unseeds or removes a repository it did not bring, whatever the open dir is made to say.
note list.tsv rows: rid, state, did, date, kilobytes, name, description, note.
global od uchar 512
global odl ulong 1
global sf uchar 512
global sfl ulong 1
global wd uchar 512
global wdl ulong 1
global sd uchar 512
global sdl ulong 1
global hd uchar 256
global hdl ulong 1
global pth uchar 1100
global pthl ulong 1
global pt2 uchar 1100
global rpk uchar 2300
global qb uchar 65536
global lb uchar 262144
global lbl ulong 1
global ob uchar 524288
global obl ulong 1
global cb uchar 65536
global cbl ulong 1
global pk uchar 4096
global pkn ulong 1
global sb uchar 1100
global sbl ulong 1
global rid uchar 48
global ridl ulong 1
global did uchar 96
global didl ulong 1
global nt uchar 208
global ntl ulong 1
global nm uchar 128
global nml ulong 1
global ds uchar 408
global dsl ulong 1
global dt uchar 16
global dtl ulong 1
global kb ulong 1
global ub uchar 408
global ubl ulong 1
global qe ulong 1
text kq "queue"
text kqold "queue.old"
text klist "list.tsv"
text kxt ".tmp"
text kout "out"
text kb58 "123456789ABCDEFGHJKLMNPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijkmnopqrstuvwxyz"
text kenv "/usr/bin/env"
text kdashi "-i"
text khome "HOME="
text kpath "PATH="
text kpath2 "/.local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin"
text krad "/.local/bin/rad"
text kseed "seed"
text kunseed "unseed"
text kinspect "inspect"
text kpayload "--payload"
text kscope "--scope"
text kall "all"
text kfetch "--fetch"
text kradp "rad:"
text kdu "/usr/bin/du"
text ksk "-sk"
text kdate "/usr/bin/date"
text ku "-u"
text kfmt "+%F"
text krm "/usr/bin/rm"
text krf "-rf"
text kdd "--"
text knull "/dev/null"
text kopen "open"
text kwith "withdrawn"
text kheld "held"
text kvis "--visibility"
text kpub "public"
text kallow "allow"
text kr0 "refused: intake is open to invited keys for now"
text kr1 "refused: this project's storage is already on this node"
text kr2 "refused: this key already has 8 open projects"
text kr3 "refused: the shelf is full"
text kr4 "refused: not found on the Radicle network (publish it, then rad sync --announce)"
text kr5 "refused: larger than 50 MiB"
text kr6 "refused: the Radicle node did not answer; try again"
text kr7 "refused: this node already seeds this project"
text kname "\"name\""
text kdesc "\"description\""
text kunnamed "unnamed project"
note ---- small helpers
fn b58 c uchar to bool
for i ulong len kb58 bound 64
if eq get kb58 i c
ret true
end
end
ret false
end
note sbz / sbt / sbg: the scratch string: empty it, append a text, append the rid
fn sbz to void
put sbl 0 0
end
fn sbc c uchar to void
o = get sbl 0
if lt o 1099
put sb o c
put sbl 0 add o 1
end
end
fn sbt t view uchar * to void
for i ulong len t bound 256
sbc get t i
end
end
fn sbrid to void
for i ulong get ridl 0 bound 44
sbc get rid i
end
end
fn sbhome to void
for i ulong get hdl 0 bound 256
sbc get hd i
end
end
fn sbstore to void
for i ulong get sdl 0 bound 512
sbc get sd i
end
sbrid
end
note ---- the packed argument list (u16 count, then per record a u16 length and the bytes)
fn pknew to void
put pkn 0 2
put pk 0 0
put pk 1 0
end
fn pkrec n ulong to ulong
o = get pkn 0
put pk o uchar and n 255
put pk add o 1 uchar shr n 8
put pk 0 uchar add get pk 0 1
ret add o 2
end
fn pkt t view uchar * to void
n = len t
o = pkrec n
for i ulong n bound 256
put pk add o i get t i
end
put pkn 0 add o n
end
note pks: the scratch string as one argument
fn pks to void
n = get sbl 0
o = pkrec n
for i ulong n bound 1100
put pk add o i get sb i
end
put pkn 0 add o n
end
note pkrad: env -i HOME=<home> PATH=<home>/.local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin <home>/.local/bin/rad
fn pkrad to void
pknew
pkt kenv
pkt kdashi
sbz
sbt khome
sbhome
pks
sbz
sbt kpath
sbhome
sbt kpath2
pks
sbz
sbhome
sbt krad
pks
end
fn pkridarg to void
sbz
sbt kradp
sbrid
pks
end
note wpath: pth = work dir + name
fn wpath name view uchar * to void
n = get wdl 0
for i ulong n bound 512
put pth i get wd i
end
for i ulong len name bound 16
put pth add n i get name i
end
put pthl 0 add n len name
end
note opath: pth = open dir + name
fn opath name view uchar * to void
n = get odl 0
for i ulong n bound 512
put pth i get od i
end
for i ulong len name bound 16
put pth add n i get name i
end
put pthl 0 add n len name
end
note child: stdin from /dev/null, stdout to <work>out, stderr to /dev/null, then the program
fn child to void
a = new uchar 4096 0
r = setpgid 0 0
fd = fopen knull 0 len knull 524288 0
if lt fd 0
exit 121
end
r = dupfd int fd 0 0
x = fclose int fd
wpath kout
r = unlink pth 0 get pthl 0
fd = fopen pth 0 get pthl 0 557249 384
if lt fd 0
exit 123
end
r = dupfd int fd 1 0
x = fclose int fd
fd = fopen knull 0 len knull 524289 0
if lt fd 0
exit 125
end
r = dupfd int fd 2 0
x = fclose int fd
n = get pkn 0
for i ulong n bound 4096
put a i get pk i
end
r = execprog a 0 n
exit 127
end
note run: the packed command with a deadline in seconds. True when it exited 0. Its stdout is in cb.
fn run secs ulong to bool
st = new uchar 4 0
put cbl 0 0
pid = fork
if lt pid 0
ret false
end
if eq pid 0
child
exit 127
end
r = setpgid int pid int pid
ok = false
for i ulong mul secs 100 bound 12000
r = waitpid int pid st 0 4 1
if eq r pid
ok = true
break
end
if lt r 0
break
end
r = sleepns 10000000
end
if not ok
r = killpid int neg pid 9
r = killpid int pid 9
for i ulong 200
r = waitpid int pid st 0 4 1
if ne r 0
break
end
r = sleepns 10000000
end
ret false
end
for i ulong 4
if ne get st i 0
ret false
end
end
wpath kout
fd = fopen pth 0 get pthl 0 557056 0
if lt fd 0
ret true
end
n = ulong 0
k = long 1
while gt k 0 bound 65536
k = read int fd cb n sub 65535 n
if gt k 0
n = add n ulong k
end
end
x = fclose int fd
put cbl 0 n
ret true
end
note ---- the commands
fn doseed to bool
pkrad
pkt kseed
pkridarg
pkt kscope
pkt kall
pkt kfetch
ret run 90
end
fn dounseed to void
pkrad
pkt kunseed
pkridarg
ok = run 30
end
fn dopayload to bool
pkrad
pkt kinspect
pkridarg
pkt kpayload
ret run 30
end
note dovis: rad inspect <rid> --visibility says public
fn dovis to bool
pkrad
pkt kinspect
pkridarg
pkt kvis
if not run 30
ret false
end
if lt get cbl 0 len kpub
ret false
end
for i ulong len kpub bound 16
if ne get cb i get kpub i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
fn dodu to bool
pknew
pkt kdu
pkt ksk
sbz
sbstore
pks
if not run 30
ret false
end
v = ulong 0
n = get cbl 0
i = ulong 0
while lt i n bound 24
c = get cb i
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
break
end
v = add mul v 10 ulong sub c 48
i = add i 1
end
put kb 0 v
ret gt i 0
end
fn dodate to void
put dtl 0 0
pknew
pkt kdate
pkt ku
pkt kfmt
if not run 10
ret
end
n = get cbl 0
if lt n 10
ret
end
for i ulong 10
c = get cb i
ok = false
if and ge c 48 le c 57
ok = true
end
if eq c 45
ok = true
end
if not ok
ret
end
put dt i c
end
put dtl 0 10
end
note dorm: remove the storage folder of the current rid. Callers have checked that this program
note brought it.
fn dorm to void
pknew
pkt krm
pkt krf
pkt kdd
sbz
sbstore
pks
ok = run 60
end
fn stored to bool
sbz
sbstore
ret eq faccess sb 0 get sbl 0 0 0
end
note jget: the string value of key t in the command output, sanitized, at most cap bytes, into
note nm (which 0) or ds (which 1). An escape becomes a space, a control byte a space.
note uin: lo <= c <= hi
fn uin c uchar lo uchar hi uchar to bool
ret and ge c lo le c hi
end
note uvalid: the length of the well-formed UTF-8 character at ub[i], or 0 (RFC 3629: no overlong
note form, no surrogate, nothing past U+10FFFF). The same rule as research/agent.om.
fn uvalid i ulong to ulong
n = get ubl 0
c = get ub i
if lt c 128
ret 1
end
if uin c 194 223
if lt add i 1 n
if uin get ub add i 1 128 191
ret 2
end
end
ret 0
end
lo = uchar 128
hi = uchar 191
if uin c 224 239
if eq c 224
lo = uchar 160
end
if eq c 237
hi = uchar 159
end
if lt add i 2 n
if and uin get ub add i 1 lo hi uin get ub add i 2 128 191
ret 3
end
end
ret 0
end
if uin c 240 244
if eq c 240
lo = uchar 144
end
if eq c 244
hi = uchar 143
end
if lt add i 3 n
if and and uin get ub add i 1 lo hi uin get ub add i 2 128 191 uin get ub add i 3 128 191
ret 4
end
end
end
ret 0
end
note usan: every byte of ub that does not start a well-formed UTF-8 character becomes "?". A name
note or description cut at its cap can end inside a character; the list and its JSON stay UTF-8.
fn usan to void
n = get ubl 0
i = ulong 0
while lt i n bound 408
k = uvalid i
if eq k 0
put ub i 63
i = add i 1
else
i = add i k
end
end
end
fn usnm to void
n = get nml 0
for i ulong n bound 120
put ub i get nm i
end
put ubl 0 n
usan
for i ulong n bound 120
put nm i get ub i
end
end
fn usds to void
n = get dsl 0
for i ulong n bound 400
put ub i get ds i
end
put ubl 0 n
usan
for i ulong n bound 400
put ds i get ub i
end
end
fn usnt to void
n = get ntl 0
for i ulong n bound 200
put ub i get nt i
end
put ubl 0 n
usan
for i ulong n bound 200
put nt i get ub i
end
end
note policy: does the node's seeding policy list (rad seed without a rid) name the current rid?
note 0 no, 1 yes, 2 the node did not answer or the list did not fit. A bring goes on only at 0, so
note it never rewrites the scope of a policy the owner set, and a failed fetch never unseeds one.
fn rmatch i ulong to bool
n = get ridl 0
for k ulong n bound 44
if ne get cb add i k get rid k
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
fn policy to ulong
pkrad
pkt kseed
if not run 30
ret 2
end
n = get cbl 0
if ge n 65535
ret 2
end
m = get ridl 0
i = ulong 0
while le add i m n bound 65536
if rmatch i
ret 1
end
i = add i 1
end
ret 0
end
fn jput which ulong o ulong c uchar to void
if eq which 0
put nm o c
else
put ds o c
end
end
fn jmatch t view uchar * i ulong to bool
for k ulong len t bound 16
if ne get cb add i k get t k
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
fn jfind t view uchar * to ulong
n = get cbl 0
m = len t
i = ulong 0
while lt add i m n bound 65536
if jmatch t i
ret add i m
end
i = add i 1
end
ret n
end
fn jget t view uchar * which ulong cap ulong to ulong
n = get cbl 0
p = jfind t
while lt p n bound 65536
if eq get cb p 34
break
end
p = add p 1
end
if ge p n
ret 0
end
p = add p 1
o = ulong 0
while lt p n bound 65536
c = get cb p
if eq c 34
break
end
if eq c 92
p = add p 1
c = uchar 32
end
if or lt c 32 eq c 127
c = uchar 32
end
if lt o cap
jput which o c
o = add o 1
end
p = add p 1
end
ret o
end
note ---- the private list.tsv in lb
fn lload to void
put lbl 0 0
wpath klist
fd = fopen pth 0 get pthl 0 557056 0
if lt fd 0
ret
end
m = ulong 0
k = long 1
while gt k 0 bound 262144
k = read int fd lb m sub 262143 m
if gt k 0
m = add m ulong k
end
end
x = fclose int fd
put lbl 0 m
end
fn leol a ulong to ulong
lim = get lbl 0
i = a
while lt i lim bound 262144
if eq get lb i 10
ret i
end
i = add i 1
end
ret lim
end
note lfe: the end of the field that starts at a in the row ending at e
fn lfe a ulong e ulong to ulong
p = a
while lt p e bound 262144
if eq get lb p 9
ret p
end
p = add p 1
end
ret e
end
note lfld: start of field k of the row s..e
fn lfld s ulong e ulong k ulong to ulong
p = s
j = ulong 0
while lt j k bound 8
p = lfe p e
if lt p e
p = add p 1
end
j = add j 1
end
ret p
end
note lisrid: the row's first field is the current rid
fn lisrid s ulong e ulong to bool
b = lfe s e
n = get ridl 0
if ne sub b s n
ret false
end
for i ulong n bound 44
if ne get lb add s i get rid i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
fn lisopen s ulong e ulong to bool
a = lfld s e 1
b = lfe a e
if ne sub b a len kopen
ret false
end
for i ulong len kopen
if ne get lb add a i get kopen i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note lisdid: the row's did (field 2) is the current did
fn lisdid s ulong e ulong to bool
a = lfld s e 2
b = lfe a e
n = get didl 0
if ne sub b a n
ret false
end
for i ulong n bound 96
if ne get lb add a i get did i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note lfind: the start of the row of the current rid, or lbl
fn lfind to ulong
lim = get lbl 0
s = ulong 0
while lt s lim bound 4096
e = leol s
if lisrid s e
ret s
end
s = add e 1
end
ret lim
end
note lstate: the state (field 1) of the row s..e is t
fn lstate s ulong e ulong t view uchar * to bool
a = lfld s e 1
b = lfe a e
if ne sub b a len t
ret false
end
for i ulong len t bound 128
if ne get lb add a i get t i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note lfailed: the private list says this program's own fetch of the current rid failed (not found
note or over the size limit). A storage folder found for it then is that fetch's leftover (the
note node can finish a fetch after rad was stopped at its deadline), not a repository of the owner.
fn lfailed to bool
s = lfind
if ge s get lbl 0
ret false
end
e = leol s
if lstate s e kr4
ret true
end
ret lstate s e kr5
end
note lpub: the row is on the shelf: open (this program fetched the project) or held (the node
note already had it; the row only lists it)
fn lpub s ulong e ulong to bool
if lisopen s e
ret true
end
ret lstate s e kheld
end
note lcount: rows on the shelf; mine true counts only the current did's
fn lcount mine bool to ulong
lim = get lbl 0
n = ulong 0
s = ulong 0
while lt s lim bound 4096
e = leol s
if lpub s e
if mine
if lisdid s e
n = add n 1
end
else
n = add n 1
end
end
s = add e 1
end
ret n
end
note ---- writing the new list
fn emb c uchar to void
o = get obl 0
if lt o 524288
put ob o c
put obl 0 add o 1
end
end
fn emt t view uchar * to void
for i ulong len t bound 256
emb get t i
end
end
fn emn v ulong to void
d = new uchar 20 0
n = ulong 0
x = v
if eq x 0
emb 48
end
while gt x 0 bound 20
put d n uchar add 48 rem x 10
x = div x 10
n = add n 1
end
while gt n 0 bound 20
n = sub n 1
emb get d n
end
end
note keep: every row but the current rid's into ob. Rows that are not open (refusals, withdrawals)
note share a budget of 65,536 bytes (held rows count as open here); the oldest of them are dropped first, so a key that is not
note invited cannot grow the list past what lload reads (262,143 bytes) and push out the rows of
note projects this program brought. Open rows are never dropped: at most 200, 887 bytes each.
fn keep to void
lim = get lbl 0
put obl 0 0
t = ulong 0
s = ulong 0
while lt s lim bound 4096
e = leol s
if and gt e s not lisrid s e
if not lpub s e
t = add t add sub e s 1
end
end
s = add e 1
end
drop = ulong 0
if gt t 65536
drop = sub t 65536
end
s = ulong 0
while lt s lim bound 4096
e = leol s
if and gt e s not lisrid s e
skip = false
if gt drop 0
if not lpub s e
skip = true
d = add sub e s 1
if gt d drop
drop = ulong 0
else
drop = sub drop d
end
end
end
if not skip
i = s
while lt i e bound 262144
emb get lb i
i = add i 1
end
emb 10
end
end
s = add e 1
end
end
note rowhead: rid, state, did, date for the current request
fn rowhead state view uchar * to void
for i ulong get ridl 0 bound 44
emb get rid i
end
emb 9
emt state
emb 9
for i ulong get didl 0 bound 96
emb get did i
end
emb 9
for i ulong get dtl 0 bound 10
emb get dt i
end
emb 9
end
note rowtail: kilobytes, name, description, note
fn rowtail to void
emn get kb 0
emb 9
for i ulong get nml 0 bound 120
emb get nm i
end
emb 9
for i ulong get dsl 0 bound 400
emb get ds i
end
emb 9
for i ulong get ntl 0 bound 200
emb get nt i
end
emb 10
end
note wr: write ob to pth + ".tmp", sync, rename onto pth
fn wr to bool
n = get pthl 0
for i ulong n bound 1100
put pt2 i get pth i
end
for i ulong len kxt
put pt2 add n i get kxt i
end
m = add n len kxt
r = unlink pt2 0 m
fd = fopen pt2 0 m 557249 420
if lt fd 0
ret false
end
z = get obl 0
o = ulong 0
ok = true
while lt o z bound 524288
k = write int fd ob o sub z o
if le k 0
ok = false
o = z
else
o = add o ulong k
end
end
r = fsync int fd
x = fclose int fd
if not ok
ret false
end
put rpk 0 2
put rpk 1 0
put rpk 2 uchar and m 255
put rpk 3 uchar shr m 8
for i ulong m bound 1100
put rpk add 4 i get pt2 i
end
o = add 4 m
put rpk o uchar and n 255
put rpk add o 1 uchar shr n 8
for i ulong n bound 1100
put rpk add add o 2 i get pth i
end
ret eq renames rpk 0 add add o 2 n 0 0
end
note save: the list with the current row in the given state: the private list first, then the
note published copy
fn save state view uchar * to void
keep
dodate
rowhead state
rowtail
wpath klist
ok = wr
opath klist
ok = wr
end
fn blank to void
put kb 0 0
put nml 0 0
put dsl 0 0
end
note allowed: <work dir>allow lists the keys that may bring a project, one DID a line; a line
note that is only * admits every signed-in key. No file admits nobody. The file is outside the
note folder forged can write.
fn aload to bool
put cbl 0 0
wpath kallow
fd = fopen pth 0 get pthl 0 557056 0
if lt fd 0
ret false
end
n = ulong 0
k = long 1
while gt k 0 bound 65536
k = read int fd cb n sub 65535 n
if gt k 0
n = add n ulong k
end
end
x = fclose int fd
put cbl 0 n
ret true
end
note aline: the allow line cb[a, e) is * or the current did
fn aline a ulong e ulong to bool
m = sub e a
if eq m 1
if eq get cb a 42
ret true
end
end
d = get didl 0
if ne m d
ret false
end
for i ulong d bound 96
if ne get cb add a i get did i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
fn aeol a ulong to ulong
n = get cbl 0
e = a
while lt e n bound 65536
if eq get cb e 10
ret e
end
e = add e 1
end
ret n
end
fn allowed to bool
if not aload
ret false
end
n = get cbl 0
a = ulong 0
while lt a n bound 4096
e = aeol a
if aline a e
ret true
end
a = add e 1
end
ret false
end
note ---- one request
note rsave: save a refusal that is not about a fetch, unless the row says this program's own fetch
note of the rid failed (fl): that row is what lets the next bring clear a late folder, so a key
note that is not invited, a full quota or a node that does not answer must not replace it.
fn rsave t view uchar * fl bool to void
if not fl
save t
end
end
note describe: name and description from the project's identity document
fn describe to void
if dopayload
put nml 0 jget kname 0 120
put dsl 0 jget kdesc 1 400
usnm
usds
end
if eq get nml 0 0
for i ulong len kunnamed bound 32
put nm i get kunnamed i
end
put nml 0 len kunnamed
end
end
fn bring to void
blank
lload
s = lfind
if lt s get lbl 0
if lpub s leol s
ret
end
end
fl = lfailed
if not allowed
rsave kr0 fl
ret
end
left = false
held = false
if stored
left = fl
if not left
held = true
end
end
if ge lcount true 8
rsave kr2 fl
ret
end
if ge lcount false 200
rsave kr3 fl
ret
end
if held
if not dovis
save kr1
ret
end
ok = dodu
describe
save kheld
ret
end
p = policy
if eq p 1
save kr7
ret
end
if eq p 2
rsave kr6 fl
ret
end
if left
dorm
end
ok = doseed
if ok
ok = stored
end
if not ok
dounseed
if stored
dorm
end
save kr4
ret
end
ok = dodu
if or not ok gt get kb 0 51200
dounseed
dorm
save kr5
ret
end
describe
save kopen
end
note withdraw: only an open or held row brought by this key. Its name, description and size are kept.
fn withdraw to void
lload
s = lfind
if ge s get lbl 0
ret
end
e = leol s
held = lstate s e kheld
if not held
if not lisopen s e
ret
end
end
if not lisdid s e
ret
end
blank
a = lfld s e 5
b = lfe a e
n = sub b a
if gt n 120
n = ulong 120
end
for i ulong n bound 120
put nm i get lb add a i
end
put nml 0 n
put ntl 0 0
if not held
dounseed
dorm
end
save kwith
end
note ---- the queue
fn getoff to ulong
b = new uchar 24 0
fd = fopen sf 0 get sfl 0 524288 0
if lt fd 0
ret 0
end
k = read int fd b 0 20
x = fclose int fd
v = ulong 0
if gt k 0
for i ulong ulong k bound 20
c = get b i
if and ge c 48 le c 57
v = add mul v 10 ulong sub c 48
end
end
end
ret v
end
fn putoff v ulong to void
put obl 0 0
emn v
emb 10
n = get sfl 0
for i ulong n bound 512
put pth i get sf i
end
put pthl 0 n
ok = wr
end
note field: copy qb[a, e) up to the next tab into rid (which 0), did (1) or the note (2); the
note index after the tab, or e. A field that breaks its rule sets its length to 0.
fn fput which ulong o ulong c uchar to void
if eq which 0
put rid o c
end
if eq which 1
put did o c
end
if eq which 2
put nt o c
end
end
fn qfield a ulong e ulong which ulong cap ulong to ulong
o = ulong 0
bad = false
p = a
while lt p e bound 65536
c = get qb p
if eq c 9
break
end
if eq which 0
if not b58 c
bad = true
end
end
if eq which 1
if or le c 32 ge c 127
bad = true
end
end
if eq which 2
if or lt c 32 eq c 127
c = uchar 32
end
end
if ge o cap
bad = true
else
fput which o c
o = add o 1
end
p = add p 1
end
if bad
o = ulong 0
end
if eq which 0
put ridl 0 o
end
if eq which 1
put didl 0 o
end
if eq which 2
put ntl 0 o
end
if lt p e
ret add p 1
end
ret e
end
note qline: qb[a, e) is one queue line. True when it was well formed and was acted on.
fn qline a ulong e ulong to bool
if lt sub e a 4
ret false
end
kind = get qb a
if ne get qb add a 1 9
ret false
end
p = qfield add a 2 e 0 44
p = qfield p e 1 96
put ntl 0 0
if eq kind 66
p = qfield p e 2 200
usnt
end
if or lt get ridl 0 20 eq get didl 0 0
ret false
end
if ne get rid 0 122
ret false
end
if eq kind 66
bring
ret true
end
if eq kind 87
withdraw
ret true
end
ret false
end
note qeol: the index of the line feed at or after a in qb[0, m), or m
fn qeol a ulong m ulong to ulong
e = a
while lt e m bound 65536
if eq get qb e 10
ret e
end
e = add e 1
end
ret m
end
note qchunk: the complete lines of one 64 KiB chunk of the queue file at pth, from the stored
note offset. The offset is saved after each line that was acted on and once at the end of the
note chunk, not after every ignored line (each save is a write, a sync and a rename). qe is 1 when the file opened and nothing was left to read.
fn qchunk to bool
put qe 0 0
fd = fopen pth 0 get pthl 0 524288 0
if lt fd 0
ret false
end
off = getoff
k = pread int fd qb 0 65536 long off
x = fclose int fd
if le k 0
put qe 0 1
ret false
end
m = ulong k
a = ulong 0
did1 = false
dirty = false
while lt a m bound 65536
e = qeol a m
if ge e m
if and eq a 0 eq m 65536
a = m
dirty = true
did1 = true
end
break
end
acted = qline a e
did1 = true
a = add e 1
if acted
putoff add off a
dirty = false
else
dirty = true
end
end
if dirty
putoff add off a
end
ret did1
end
note qrotate: rename <open dir>queue to queue.old. forged creates a new queue at its next request,
note so the queue never stays at forged's 1 MiB cap once this program has read it.
fn qrotate to bool
opath kqold
m = get pthl 0
for i ulong m bound 1100
put pt2 i get pth i
end
opath kq
n = get pthl 0
put rpk 0 2
put rpk 1 0
put rpk 2 uchar and n 255
put rpk 3 uchar shr n 8
for i ulong n bound 1100
put rpk add 4 i get pth i
end
o = add 4 n
put rpk o uchar and m 255
put rpk add o 1 uchar shr m 8
for i ulong m bound 1100
put rpk add add o 2 i get pt2 i
end
ret eq renames rpk 0 add add o 2 m 0 0
end
note qold: finish a rotated queue. The stored offset is one into queue.old while it exists and is
note above 0 (a rotation happens only past 262,144 bytes); 0 means it was finished before a
note restart, so it is only removed. Any line forged appended during the rename is read here.
fn qold to bool
opath kqold
if ne faccess pth 0 get pthl 0 0 0
ret false
end
if gt getoff 0
for i ulong 4096
opath kqold
if not qchunk
break
end
end
end
putoff 0
opath kqold
r = unlink pth 0 get pthl 0
ret eq r 0
end
note qpass: one pass. A queue read to its end past 262,144 bytes is rotated; the second of sleep
note lets a request forged opened before the rename finish its write before queue.old is read.
fn qpass to bool
if qold
ret true
end
opath kq
if qchunk
ret true
end
if eq get qe 0 0
ret false
end
if lt getoff 262144
ret false
end
if not qrotate
ret false
end
z = sleepns 1000000000
ret true
end
note argp: argument i into its buffer; its length
fn aput i ulong k ulong c uchar to void
if eq i 1
put od k c
end
if eq i 2
put sf k c
end
if eq i 3
put wd k c
end
if eq i 4
put sd k c
end
if eq i 5
put hd k c
end
end
fn argp i ulong cap ulong to ulong
b = new uchar 512 0
n = argread i b 0 cap
if le n 0
ret 0
end
m = ulong n
for k ulong m bound 512
aput i k get b k
end
ret m
end
fn slashed i ulong to bool
if eq i 1
ret eq get od sub get odl 0 1 47
end
if eq i 3
ret eq get wd sub get wdl 0 1 47
end
ret eq get sd sub get sdl 0 1 47
end
fn main to int
if lt argcnt 6
ret 2
end
put odl 0 argp 1 500
put sfl 0 argp 2 500
put wdl 0 argp 3 500
put sdl 0 argp 4 500
put hdl 0 argp 5 250
if eq get odl 0 0
ret 2
end
if eq get sfl 0 0
ret 2
end
if eq get wdl 0 0
ret 2
end
if eq get sdl 0 0
ret 2
end
if eq get hdl 0 0
ret 2
end
if not slashed 1
ret 2
end
if not slashed 3
ret 2
end
if not slashed 4
ret 2
end
once = gt argcnt 6
while true bound 9223372036854775807
did1 = qpass
if once
if not did1
ret 0
end
else
if not did1
z = sleepns 1000000000
end
end
end
ret 0
end
